# gen_fu_generator_fix_sweep: the four generator fixes measured in simulation, before and after

WHAT THIS CLAIMS. Every declared bin of gen_test_bit_ratified and gen_test_cmp_zca is hit at
every one of forty seeds with the handed generators, where the same seeds on the same manifests
left nine bins short before them; and the WARL backstop's four new programs run. NOT claimed:
anything about a bin these two entries do not declare, and nothing about the round's coverage,
which no unmeasured sweep can speak to. Every figure below was read by me from the run
directories named here, not taken from a report.

PROVENANCE, and why before and after are one measurement.
  post-fix runs   /proj_soc/user_dev/fzhang/ibex_dv_out/regress_gsfix2/runs
  pre-fix runs    /proj_soc/user_dev/fzhang/ibex_dv_out/regress_gensweep2/runs
  The seed sets are identical set for set in both sweeps, 40 and 40 for each entry.
  Each entry's fcov_manifest_used.yaml carries ONE md5 across all its runs in both sweeps, and
  that md5 equals the committed manifest, so the bar did not move between them.

THE BUILDS ARE NOT THE SAME, which is the honest caveat and the reason for a control. The fix
root was archived from a later HEAD, so the two sweeps built different testbench sources. The
control is below: the three covergroups these bins live on, and the sampler call sites that feed
them, are byte-identical across the two roots, so the testbench delta cannot account for the
change. That makes this a controlled comparison of the generators, not a single-variable one of
the whole tree.

